    - initiative: "Anomaly Perception Monitoring (APM)"
        strategic_pillars:
        - Risk Management & Compliance
        - Innovation & Digital Transformation
        - Sustainable Growth
        outcome: >
        Detect and track emotionally perceived anomalies in transactional UX before they escalate into regulatory exposure or customer churn.
        metrics:
        - Trust Risk Signal Index (new KPI; baseline to be established in pilot)
        - Regulatory Escalation Lag Time (from signal to resolution)
        - Churn Risk Spike Post-Anomaly (% of users showing negative signals post-perception event)
        explanation: >
        This initiative translates emotional perception into operational foresight — proactively flagging trust-damaging experiences invisible to backend logic. It introduces a new KPI category for FinTech emotional telemetry, aligning with GLBA and internal audit readiness. It balances innovation and compliance while protecting retention. Ideal for ownership by cross-functional Trust Ops, Risk, and Data Science teams.
